<title>FRANCE: G7 to make positive statement on EMU.</title>
<headline>G7 to make positive statement on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Group of Seven rich nations are expected to make a positive statement about the launch of the single European currency at their summit in Denver this weekend, a spokeswoman for French President Jacques Chirac said on Thursday.</p>
<p>She told a news conference the Group of Seven would discuss formally for the first time in Denver Europe's plans to launch a single currency in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;Everyone considers this a realistic and credible event,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>This would be reflected in the G7 statement.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be an observation which will be very clearly positive,&quot; she said.</p>
</text>
